{"title":"1960 AHSME Problems/Problem 11","text":"<div class=\"mw-content-ltr mw-parser-output\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem\">Problem</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1960_AHSME_Problems/Problem_11&amp;action=edit&amp;section=1\" title=\"Edit section: Problem\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>For a given value of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/c/3/8c325612684d41304b9751c175df7bcc0f61f64f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$k$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"12\" height=\"14\" /> the product of the roots of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/0/6/c06e40c877e2e649a51f240863cf4593762a870f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x^2-3kx+2k^2-1=0$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"182\" height=\"16\" />\nis <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/0/a/e0a0db32027a732ac57d37ef2ae9bb150f65b108.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$7$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" />. The roots may be characterized as:\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/4/b/e4b0128b2c2c19666e6e42093f28e1bf6af3cc2f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\textbf{(A) }\\text{integral and positive} \\qquad\\textbf{(B) }\\text{integral and negative} \\qquad \\\\ \\textbf{(C) }\\text{rational, but not integral} \\qquad\\textbf{(D) }\\text{irrational} \\qquad\\textbf{(E) } \\text{imaginary}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"492\" height=\"37\" />\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution\">Solution</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1960_AHSME_Problems/Problem_11&amp;action=edit&amp;section=2\" title=\"Edit section: Solution\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>If the product of the roots are <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/0/a/e0a0db32027a732ac57d37ef2ae9bb150f65b108.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$7$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" />, then by <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Vieta%27s_formulas\" title=\"Vieta&#39;s formulas\">Vieta's formulas</a>, \n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/0/c/c0c3333c39193ed9c82a2c1d8614462df0f82b19.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[2k^2-1=7\\]\" width=\"90\" height=\"15\" />\nSolve for <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/c/3/8c325612684d41304b9751c175df7bcc0f61f64f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$k$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"12\" height=\"14\" /> in the resulting equation to get\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/c/d/1cd6df4d9d808a623f22dc841ef903a6b01cd1c1.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[2k^2=8\\]\" width=\"59\" height=\"15\" />\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/6/4/4646a39d57b77763bb40188214fa33f2f3452f30.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[k^2=4\\]\" width=\"50\" height=\"15\" />\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/6/e/46e1269909a413132acf81c55772bd4ac7296bbd.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[k=\\pm 2\\]\" width=\"56\" height=\"13\" />\nThat means the two quadratics are <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/4/2/242d2ea9d50a67e3a67b8ec3e9c6e856968d6c3a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x^2-6x+7=0$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"123\" height=\"16\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/3/a/63aea38fbe42c2001281c19de85eda6a18907e56.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x^2+6x+7=0$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"123\" height=\"16\" />.  Since <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/1/d/a1d03c3c5b9abf1bdb0c9df06fe5fb11ae13d0e8.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$b^2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"17\" height=\"17\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/7/d/c7d457e388298246adb06c587bccd419ea67f7e8.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"10\" />, and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/3/7/3372c1cb6d68cf97c2d231acc0b47b95a9ed04cc.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$c$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"10\" height=\"10\" /> are the same, the <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Discriminant\" title=\"Discriminant\">discriminant</a> of both is\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/6/9/5695d622b1598eb176c1a36f506abc8d21561f1e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$36-(4 \\cdot 1 \\cdot 7) = 8$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"141\" height=\"18\" />.  Because <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/4/5/8455f3b5cb3b4880b8c9d782a5c1f0334db819eb.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$8$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> is not a perfect square, the roots for both are irrational, so the answer is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/9/3/693c4044f8526a8179956e8ac7a3f2f9d61e2c1c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\boxed{\\textbf{(D)}}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -11px\" width=\"43\" height=\"30\" />.\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"See_Also\">See Also</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1960_AHSME_Problems/Problem_11&amp;action=edit&amp;section=3\" title=\"Edit section: See Also\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<table class=\"wikitable\" style=\"margin:0.5em auto; font-size:95%; border:1px solid black; width:80%;\">\n<tbody><tr>\n<td style=\"background:#ccf;text-align:center;\" colspan=\"3\"><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1960_AHSME\" title=\"1960 AHSME\">1960 AHSC</a></b> (<b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1960_AHSME_Problems\" title=\"1960 AHSME Problems\">Problems</a></b> • <b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1960_AHSME_Answer_Key\" title=\"1960 AHSME Answer Key\">Answer Key</a></b> • <a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"http://www.artofproblemsolving.com/Forum/resources.php?c=182&amp;cid=44&amp;year=1960\">Resources</a>)\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td width=\"50%\" align=\"center\" rowspa